y to protect them  the third initiative we will launch is  on innovation  innovation is key  to fight climate change and to progress  into a circular economy  with clean  for producing procedures and more  sustainable  consumption  and therefore future technologies will  be the key to help cut emissions  we want to demonstrate  and this is the core of this initiative  that investment in green innovations  pays off  so in glasgow i will launch together  with bill gates a program called  breakthrough energy catalyst  we join forces there  the aim is to prove that if you have a  breakthrough innovation of course at the  very beginning it's a bit more expensive  but if we relieve that green premium we  help this  innovation  to be more  to be more fast and being market  feasible and to scale up better at the  markets such as for example  innovation in clean hydrogen sustainable  aviation fuels carbon storage  carbon capture and the energy storage  such to name  the four fields where we will be  investing in  last but not least the  fifth initiative that we will presumably  start we're still working on it  that is joining the us the uk germany  france and the european union  to launch together with south africa a  just energy transition partnership  the idea is  that  the countries  support south africa  to phase out of coal faster and to go  earlier and faster into developing  renewables  we're still working on that but  i am confident that we are going to  launch this new proposal and then this  partnership  could become a template on how to  support just transitions around the  globe with sponsoring countries and  countries that have to move on faster in  the just transition  that was  quite a bit sorry for being a bit long  but it's important four days ahead of us  and back to you donna  thank you very much president i will  take a few questions  alternating between the room and the  colleagues connected online and there  are many of them there irini first go  ahead 