ectations are not very high if we  look at the national country  contributions are not enough to keep  global warming below two percent and the  financial contributions are falling  short of what we need to be achieved so  having this in mind what is your best  hope for  the cop 26  and then also if you expect a deal on  article 6 carbon offset trading rule  book  during the climate summit  so indeed the starting point is not a  good one  and in therefore it's also a moment of  truth to science tells us very clearly  and the reports tell us very clearly  you're not where you want to be in  fighting climate change you have to get  better  and the second message is  it's not a question of 30 40 years it's  now it's this decade where we have to  get better otherwise we reach we risk to  reach irreversible tipping points  and then  um it is very clear that this is a high  ambition with leadership where we have  to go into cop26 it's encouraging the  negotiators  really to set the bar high  it's not about the question who is going  to be  more advanced than  others it's a question of survival of  mankind on this planet it's the question  of how we gonna leave this world behind  to our children it's a question about  are we gonna now do the necessary steps  or are we running more and more  into extreme weather situation as we've  seen this summer they will increase and  thus also block more and more resources  in  in fixing the damages  instead of being able in investing into  the innovation that is necessary to  really get better  thank you very much i will now go  towards the colleagues connected online  by patrizia has her hand up first on the  list  thank you dana from the floor and good  afternoon president  um i would like to understand what you  expect from the g20 and how do you  assess your cooperation with premier  draghi  uh during the italian  g20 presidency thank you  yes the the cooperation uh with madrid  and is excellent  um i want to recall that we have t